{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{ph}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Sch_{ph}$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Sch$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\Sch/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0009": "$S/S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fibre-products-ph}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3c8eca64f879e8f7199374359c92fa8507cd088526a03eb21dae104abb1d0955", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9ee0123b49397c1365db199c030826a171aa59396c1c736d21a5825e97864e49", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a big ph\nsite containing <MATH_0003>. The underlying categories of the sites\n<MATH_0004>, <MATH_0005>, and <MATH_0006> have fibre products.\nIn each case the obvious functor into the category <MATH_0007> of\nall schemes commutes with taking fibre products. The category\n<MATH_0008> has a final object, namely <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c1fad111f67f1779bfc9c8493dcf79db6fcaa9bc49314f7cb54c2a693b5a79a8", "unit_id": "tag:0DBN:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Sch_{ph}$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\to U$", "MATH_0004": "$W \\to U$", "MATH_0005": "$U, V, W \\in \\Ob(\\Sch_{ph})$", "MATH_0006": "$V \\times_U W$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Sch_{ph}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Sch$", "MATH_0009": "$V/S$", "MATH_0010": "$W/S$", "MATH_0011": "$U/S$", "MATH_0012": "$S$", "MATH_0013": "$(\\Sch/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0014": "$(\\Sch/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0015": "$U, V, W$", "MATH_0016": "$V \\times_U W$", "MATH_0017": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sets-lemma-what-is-in-it}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ee565a8ca25c1d76ffa2f561731b642e366a771d9195c0a1414b37764b85ed25", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f39149a3e7898dd0e4888c73dfa4d97b488cc87b2db1a9f4ac64e23f5d14b214", "source_text": "For <MATH_0001> it is true by construction, see\nSets, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nSuppose we have <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> morphisms\nof schemes with <MATH_0005>.\nThe fibre product <MATH_0006> in <MATH_0007>\nis a fibre product in <MATH_0008> and\nis the fibre product of <MATH_0009> with <MATH_0010> over <MATH_0011> in\nthe category of all schemes over <MATH_0012>, and hence also a\nfibre product in <MATH_0013>.\nThis proves the result for <MATH_0014>.\nIf <MATH_0015> are affine, so is <MATH_0016> and hence the\nresult for <MATH_0017>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f41aebdd466242fd28cc4e09fdbc00ed406926d2acaf8b26b8b7904821885dac", "unit_id": "tag:0DBN:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5954d6bc189fcd6a5b067571dcd7f28f72aeb338642c7355d7f2948fadc819c0", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext, we check that the big affine site defines the same\ntopos as the big site.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:78c6b1773b894b6b6a83aad54cff4dcbe080120f2b8498c883a3a9768e16ad14", "unit_id": "tag:0DBC:prose-0007"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{ph}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Sh((\\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sh((\\Sch/S)_{ph})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-affine-big-site-ph}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7449e9745933206a915345bd25fa0f7ee7415d6c33d18f36903408f188174403", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8a0ec54fd1435062c5e6cc37b42ccfddc0b3b50261bdfdf8d240eb3916f86659", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a big ph\nsite containing <MATH_0003>.\nThe functor <MATH_0004>\nis cocontinuous and induces an equivalence of topoi from\n<MATH_0005> to\n<MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:936c19b23e16267322fd366b0308cc15c7bd77dfe1354c06693bf2fd09809c81", "unit_id": "tag:0DBP:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DBC", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u : (\\textit{Aff}/S)_{ph} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{ph}$", "MATH_0002": "$T/S$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$u$", "MATH_0006": "$u$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-special-cocontinuous-functor}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-lemma-equivalence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a55af885bfc428c4a64005c8d561b51eb909955804dbb4f6819ea172f72b9903", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c2d5b99a6b830e4d8d6e3a19b3c9353bce8b64b01bd3c2bc1772ebe14f23c39d", "source_text": "The notion of a special cocontinuous functor is introduced in\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\nThus we have to verify assumptions (1) -- (5) of\nSites, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nDenote the inclusion functor\n<MATH_0001>.\nBeing cocontinuous follows because any ph covering of\n<MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> affine, can be refined by a standard ph covering of <MATH_0004>\nby definition. Hence (1) holds. We see <MATH_0005> is continuous simply\nbecause a finite ph covering of an affine by affines is a ph covering.\nHence (2) holds.\nParts (3) and (4) follow immediately from the fact that <MATH_0006> is\nfully faithful. And finally condition (5) follows from the\nfact that every scheme has an affine open covering (which is\na ph covering).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6c9c2bd351d555ba3032e145bcb1b8d3a7f563e9f32966e2074d45fcb2f81474", "unit_id": "tag:0DBP:proof"}
